subject: fix(streaming): stop forcing stream when client omits it — fixes [DONE] leak in JSON responses

CAUGHT BY E2E BROWSER TEST (production standalone + mock upstream):

Symptom: a request WITHOUT a stream field returned valid JSON with a
literal "data: [DONE]\n\n" appended, breaking JSON.parse for clients
(e.g. AI SDK, curl, simple HTTP consumers).

Root cause (debug-traced):
1. chatCore.js: `stream = providerRequiresStreaming ? true : (body.stream !== false)`
   → client omitting stream got stream=true (forced upstream SSE)
2. Mock received stream:false (translator/executor normalized it) → returned JSON
3. handleForcedSSEToJson correctly returned null (content-type was
   application/json, not SSE)
4. Code fell through to the streaming path (stream=true) → piped the JSON
   body through the SSE transform → wrapped as SSE chunks + appended [DONE]

Fix: `stream = body.stream === true` — only stream upstream when the
client EXPLICITLY requested it (or provider requires streaming via
forceStream). A client that omits stream now gets a true JSON response.

Also verified: explicit stream:true still returns exactly one [DONE]
(passthrough duplicate-[DONE] fix in open-sse/utils/stream.js from a
parallel agent's commit is confirmed working — streamDoneSent tracking).

Tests: full suite 1692 passed / 88 pre-existing baseline failures (no new
regressions). E2E: no-stream → clean JSON; stream:true → exactly 1 [DONE].

Refs: learnings/2026-08-06-sse-done-duplicate-leak.md (parallel agent's
postmortem of the passthrough duplicate); OpenRouter SSE protocol
(https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/streaming\)


